al downside for states  offering big prizes  still looms as it appears increasingly  likely boosters will be needed to  maintain  protection from the virus we talk about  the spoonful of sugar helping the  medicine go down but if you can only get  people to take the medicine with the  sugar you have habituated them to that  we might  be creating a precedent now for  something that can be expensive  and potentially inefficient in the  future setting a precedent doesn't worry  governor dewine who's focused on getting  shots in arms now  ss state still lags behind the national  average not every decision we've made  has been right  but it's been based on you know the  best facts that we could gather and so  are we going to offer this in the future  i don't know but  you know we're going to continue to do  what it takes  to knock this virus down as she did with  her initial vaccination  naggy says she won't wait for an  incentive before getting a booster  yeah i definitely wouldn't expect it but  if you know if it happened  great happy correlation
 

